      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: one event was created after Pending Close\n\nFor Modine’s Racine operation, manufacturing order **MO-25-09-1070** maps to work order **WO-2025-09-004** (Cooler Plate Pack). Its component-issue event was created **75 minutes after** the September cost period entered Pending Close.\n\n| Audit item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | **CE-250904-0004** |\n| Event type | **INPUT — component issue** |\n| Amount | **USD 284,763.42** — 28,476,342 cents |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T19:15:00** |\n| September Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes** — 4,500 seconds |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\n*Timestamps are reproduced exactly as stored; the source records do not specify a time zone.*\n\n### Policy conclusion\n\nThe recorded **POSTED** status is **not consistent** with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment for this newly created transaction.\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* section states that transactions created after Pending Close, even when related to the current or a prior period, **won’t be processed**. Such transactions are held until the period is closed or reopened. The documented exceptions are revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments; this **INPUT/component-issue event is not one of those exceptions**.\n\n**Sources:** `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events` from `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B policy excerpt, **PDF page 233 / printed page 225**.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**. The audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_85c0bb4450b2/audit-report.json`, and the submitted report was verified.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
